From 2f0663b599f609d887c255d2bda62db78bed44e1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 20:28:16 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] fix(desktop): page the Archived view instead of reading the
 whole archive

The Archived sidebar view and Settings > Archived sessions read every
archived row before listing any. On 2026-11-17 the three connected
gateways held 16,899 archived rows (15,432 of them auto-archived bot runs
in the mini's bb-* profiles), which is 34 pages of 500. The Electron
merge re-reads the prefix for each page, so pages took 12 s, 12 s, 16 s,
35 s and rising; the load never finished and the view stayed on "No
sessions match these filters" with no sign it was loading.

Why it was not caught: every loader test used an archive of at most
three pages, and the only state the sidebar drew for a running load was
the filtered-empty text.

- sidebar-archive: createArchivedPager() reads one page per next(), with
  the same dedupe and stop rule as before. loadArchivedSessions() reads
  the first page and publishes it; loadMoreArchivedSessions() adds one
  page; a refresh re-reads as many pages as the user loaded. A load-more
  asked for during a refresh is read by that refresh. When the list was
  edited in place (archive, unarchive, delete) the next load-more reads
  again from the top, because the server offsets have shifted.
- sidebar: Archived gets the load-more row (one page per click, also
  under project grouping, not disabled by a background refresh) and
  skeletons only while it holds no row at all.
- settings: the archived list shows the first page and a Load more
  button, re-reads from the top after an unarchive or delete, and no
  longer lists live pins the server back-fills onto an archived page.

Tests: sidebar-archive.test.ts (first page of a 16,899-row archive is
published after one request; load-more, refresh, failure, scope switch
and round trip, edit before and during a load-more, load-more during a
refresh), chat-sidebar.integration.test.tsx (rows + load-more row under
project grouping, one page per click, no filtered-empty text while
loading), sessions-settings.test.tsx (first page, Load more, re-read
after unarchive, no live pins).

Not changed and not tested here: each deeper page still costs more in
the Electron merge (it re-reads the prefix), bot rows still share the
pages with the user's own chats, a refresh that arrives while a load is
running is still dropped, and the settings list does not follow a
connection switch while it is open.

